MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Admin UI for manual payment verification flow:

1. integration-editor.tsx (WA section):
   - Add 'Nomor WhatsApp Admin' field (placeholder 6281234567890)
   - Saved to IntegrationConfig.wa_admin_phone (normalized: strip
     non-digits in API route)
   - Included in handleSave + handleTestWa payloads
   - Disabled when WA disabled

2. order-editor.tsx (admin orders list):
   - Add filter option 'Perlu Verifikasi Pembayaran' (filters
     payment.status = pending_verification via new payment_status
     query param)
   - Show payment status badge next to order status:
     * green 'Lunas' when paid
     * amber 'Perlu Verifikasi' when pending_verification
     * muted for other statuses
   - Show 'Konfirmasi Bayar' button (replaces status dropdown) when
     payment.status = pending_verification → calls /api/admin/orders/
     [id]/verify-payment → marks paid + WA customer
   - handleVerifyPayment + verifyingId loading state

3. orders.ts: extend OrderWithItems with optional 'payment' field
   (id, method, status, amount, vaNumber, vaBank, paidAt). Backward
   compatible — payment is null when not fetched.

4. /api/admin/orders GET: attach payment info to each order via
   batched findMany (one query for all orders on page). No Prisma
   relation added (schema kept gateway-agnostic). Support
   payment_status query param for filtering by payment status
   (post-fetch filter — pagination imprecise for this filter but
   acceptable since admin verifies handful at a time).

Verified: 6 API tests pass — admin login, checkout test order,
customer 'sudah bayar' (pending_verification), filter
payment_status=pending_verification returns 1 order with correct
payment attached, GET /api/admin/orders includes payment, lint
clean (0 errors).
